\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{2}{Hierarchical GNN architecture. A full 1{,}000-node mesh graph passes through a 3-layer node GIN (hidden 256) to produce per-node embeddings. Nodes are assigned to $k{=}64$ geodesic patches; mean+max pooling within each patch yields 64 super-node embeddings. A 2-layer patch GIN with max readout produces the graph embedding, which is classified by an MLP head into 99 protein-family classes}{figure.caption.4}{}}
